<div class="product-guide">
<section class="section">
  <div class="section-head"><p>Product guide</p><h1>Manage accounts, transactions and cash days</h1><p>ClassicFin Hub helps finance teams record operations, manage funded accounts and reconcile their books. Access follows the tenant's active modules and each staff member's role.</p></div>
  <div class="feature-grid">
    <article class="feature-card"><h2>Tenant and branch setup</h2><p>Platform administrators publish plans and provision tenant workspaces. Tenant owners manage branch assignments, staff access and module requests. Owners and auditors can view Main, another branch or All branches. Daily transactions retain the operator's assigned operating branch.</p></article>
    <article class="feature-card"><h2>Wallets and actual funds</h2><p>Set up cash drawers, bank funds, mobile wallets and foreign currency accounts as permitted by the subscription. The owner records the actual starting money to make an account ready and can add new business money later. A transfer between existing accounts records the same movement in both accounts.</p></article>
    <article class="feature-card"><h2>Daily entry</h2><p>Mobile money entry uses the configured wallet and payment-account defaults. Wallet settings define fee treatment. The book records the source, operator and exact currency amounts; an informational fee is not assumed to have reached cash or a network wallet.</p></article>
    <article class="feature-card"><h2>Cash day and reconciliation</h2><p>Use Cash day for opening and closing counts. When actual money differs from the book, the owner confirms the counted balance and records the difference from the account or Cash day. The adjustment preserves the original entries.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="section">
  <div class="section-head"><p>Operating modules</p><h2>What the financial books record</h2></div>
  <div class="feature-grid">
    <article class="feature-card"><h3>Mobile money</h3><p>Cash-in and cash-out record network wallet and payment effects. A supported SMS can attach its dated agent balance for review. Manual entry remains available.</p></article>
    <article class="feature-card"><h3>Banking</h3><p>Permission-checked manual deposits, withdrawals and internal account transfers post funded account movements and customer liabilities together. A masked external bank reference alone is an instruction, not an internal customer balance.</p></article>
    <article class="feature-card"><h3>Forex</h3><p>Manual buy and sell movements use a locked, duly approved rate. Foreign stock and settlement amounts remain in their respective currencies, with explicit fee treatment.</p></article>
    <article class="feature-card"><h3>Money transfer</h3><p>Reviewed manual collection records funds and a transfer payable. The payout PIN is revealed once. A checked PIN and receiver details support a separately reviewed manual payout.</p></article>
    <article class="feature-card"><h3>Expenses</h3><p>Approved expenses debit the selected funds account. Controlled corrections and voids keep the original and record linked reversals or replacements.</p></article>
    <article class="feature-card"><h3>Reports and analytics</h3><p>General reports summarize posted transactions and results by module and currency for the selected day, week, month or date range. Authorized CSV exports and browser printing keep unlike currencies and proposed instructions separate from posted movements.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="section" id="loan-management">
  <div class="section-head"><p>Manual operations · Individual activation</p><h2>Loan Management</h2><p>Use an existing customer record for loan applications, independent owner/manager review, explicit funded disbursement, repayment allocation to outstanding interest and principal, overdue tracking and audit-linked reversals. The system records actual externally performed payouts; it does not automatically send funds. Entitlement and pricing require platform administrator agreement.</p></div>
</section>
<section class="section" id="airtime">
  <div class="section-head"><p>Manual operations · Individual activation</p><h2>Airtime</h2><p>Configure telecom denominations, purchase stock against actual funds accounts, record operator-confirmed airtime sales and acquisition-cost gross profit, and preserve original entries with independently reviewed reversals. Airtime delivery is performed outside the platform; no telecom top-up API is connected.</p></div>
</section>
<section class="section">
  <div class="section-head"><p>Manual and SMS-assisted entry</p><h2>Choose how records arrive</h2></div>
  <div class="feature-grid">
    <article class="feature-card"><h3>Manual operation</h3><p>Staff enter the customer and operation details. Owners create accounts, add funds and check balances from the business accounts page. Entries follow the configured fee policy and available book balance.</p></article>
    <article class="feature-card"><h3>Android SMS capture</h3><p>A separately subscribed, configured Android gateway forwards signed messages. Supported confirmation wording can create traceable records. Unknown wording stays in the capture inbox for review; this is not universal provider-message recognition.</p></article>
    <article class="feature-card"><h3>Operating boundaries</h3><p>Manual books and SMS confirmations do not establish live provider balances or automated settlement. Live provider connections, outbound delivery and host-specific operational validation must be assessed for the intended deployment.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="section">
  <div class="section-head"><p>Plans and access</p><h2>Review the published terms before setup</h2><p>Current prices, module inclusions and workspace limits are listed on the pricing and comparison pages. Manual subscription grants are access decisions, not proof that a payment was collected.</p></div>
  <div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-dark" href="/pricing">Published pricing</a><a class="btn btn-light" href="/price-compare">Compare plans</a><a class="btn btn-light" href="/support">Contact support</a></div>
  <p>Customer data, financial records, staff accounts, invitation links and authenticated dashboards are private. Tenant records use separate logical databases within the configured deployment; that does not imply a dedicated cluster for every tenant.</p>
</section>

</div>
